                <pb facs="0194" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.152/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-20T17:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1926—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:28 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Your 25, July 12, 3 p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs states that his
                    Government is prepared to enter into negotiations for a treaty as proposed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
